cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  CrossDraft: draw a cipher once, check it twice
message: >-
  If you use this software in research, please cite it. Replace the
  placeholder author with your own details before making the repository
  public; the DOI is assigned by Zenodo on the first public release.
type: software
authors:
  - name: The CrossDraft Authors
repository-code: "https://github.com/fifstorm/crossdraft"
abstract: >-
  CrossDraft connects Digital, a schematic-capture logic simulator, to
  CLAASP, a library for automated cryptanalysis. A block cipher is drawn
  once as a circuit; Digital's simulator checks it against the published
  test vectors, and the same circuit is translated into a CLAASP model for
  differential analysis. Because neither description is transcribed by
  hand, the two cannot quietly disagree — which is the failure mode that
  hand-written analysis models hide.
keywords:
  - cryptanalysis
  - block cipher
  - differential cryptanalysis
  - SAT solving
  - reproducible research
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
